{"title":"1992 OIM Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262f27a82e4eb88e140083b9b1e59b227de78306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; a_3 &lt; \\cdots &lt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" /> and the function:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb3b28e005214b8b860c79ba8f7995604c9b6d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = \\frac{a_1}{x+a_1}+\\frac{a_2}{x+a_2}+\\cdots +\\frac{a_n}{x+a_n}\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Determine the sum of the lengths of the intervals, disjoint two by two, formed by all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d2a273ecd239f0cc9334d3134539a0174b4df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/702cfe61a123a1ed2d8d28a1eb7a5a06ffcdf31a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; a_3 &lt; \\cdots &lt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"17\" />, we can plot <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> to visualize what we're looking for:\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1992_OIM_P2b.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/21/1992_OIM_P2b.png/800px-1992_OIM_P2b.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"423\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/21/1992_OIM_P2b.png/1200px-1992_OIM_P2b.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/2/21/1992_OIM_P2b.png/1600px-1992_OIM_P2b.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Notice that the intervals will be: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc14e5c12a2ee5ac7ce9d47aac72d299cdb3ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_1=r_1-(-a_1), I_2=r_2-(-a_2), \\cdots , I_n=r_n-(-a_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"427\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus the sum of the intervals will be: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add968e822fc2bf4f0c1e73648db0851ae41e51f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i}^{}\\left( r_i+a_i \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"96\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Now we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/224ae5ff2e22575ba5a41f26a68c2c5fdc0d502d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/92107ddefd5619fd9e60e09efd442097a776cef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{\\sum_{j\\ne i}^{}\\left( a_i \\prod_{j}^{}\\left(x+a_j  \\right)\\right)}{\\prod_{i}^{}\\left(  x+a_i\\right)}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"272\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p>And solve for zero:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/399ff851ce0059fb5793cff7ace5d0896e3f2989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i}^{}\\left(  x+a_i\\right)-\\sum_{j \\ne i}^{}\\left( a_i \\prod_{j}^{}\\left(x+a_j  \\right)\\right)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -26px\" width=\"309\" height=\"58\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374b78ba7e34a6f91388cde61b9cf5820bcfedc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( x^n+\\sum_{i}^{}a_ix^{n-1}+K_{n-2}x^{n-2}+\\cdots+K_1x+K_0\\right)-\\left( \\sum_{i}^{}a_ix^{n-1}+L_{n-2}x^{n-2}+\\cdots+L_1x+L_0\\right)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"795\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c7cd35f9f0f8fa1c64728f8f6e931ba2f38304.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n+\\left( \\sum_{i}^{}a_i-\\sum_{i}^{}a_i \\right)x^{n-1}+\\left( K_{n-2}-L_{n-2} \\right)x^{n-2}+\\cdots+\\left( K_{1}-L_{1} \\right)x+\\left( K_{0}-L_{0} \\right)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"692\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d3052d0bd6242bec44973f62614ad4fbee840388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df66d9f3deecddce3e90ce33836dd65e605ed7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are coefficients of the respective polynomials for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65a6467332273f4d68d2b564d2019cf94b42104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^i$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e56e871e8b679e8fcf2a92e1cc53a96395d2b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n+(0)x^{n-1}+\\left( K_{n-2}-L_{n-2} \\right)x^{n-2}+\\cdots+\\left( K_{1}-L_{1} \\right)x+\\left( K_{0}-L_{0} \\right)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"574\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>From properties of polynomials, we know that the sum of the roots of a polynomial of degree n is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a43a7ab294bde996d60c9491ed7a9383de01d58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b/a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca004b855d662786125d522d6b7c55a3ca5f975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{n-1}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c72f3acf1f7744cfe76edaf47e45d62432cf28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4759f21f28129762da131d478e800149585c0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i}^{}r_i=-0/1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"143\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>and, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/f/d3f194b532a04635086020d79446e2f7ba871f47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i}^{}\\left( r_i+a_i \\right)=\\sum_{i}^{}r_i+\\sum_{i}^{}a_i=\\sum_{i}^{}a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"297\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Thus the sum of the intervals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/3523d1642e551e6cddbc207ce945ffcb8512d048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i}^{}a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"46\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note.  I actually competed at this event in Venezuela when I was in High School representing Puerto Rico.  I got a ZERO on this one because I didn't even know what was I supposed to do, nor did I know what the sum of the lengths of the intervals, disjoint two by two meant.  I didn't even get points for drawing the function.  haha.  Several decades ago I was able to finally solve it.  But even now, I'm still unsure about the \"disjunct two by two\" wording...</li></ul>\n<p>~Tomas Diaz. ~orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_OIM_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=OIM_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"OIM Problems and Solutions\">OIM Problems and Solutions</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe7.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe7.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183444\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 141/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 344/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5195/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.528      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n100.00%    5.528      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26076:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183444 and revision id 208218. Rendering was triggered b